//BACKBITER SPEAR +3 - 2000mo//
COPY "rick_bigg_mod/items/SPER03.itm" "override"
	SAY NAME1 "Spear"
	SAY UNIDENTIFIED_DESC "One of the earliest weapons, dating back to the most primitive of times, the first spears were simply wooden poles or sticks sharpened at one end. When the civilized races mastered metals, spearheads were made from iron and steel. Having reached this end, weaponsmiths began experimenting with different types of spearheads, thus leading to the development of certain polearm types.

STATISTICS:

Damage: 1d8 (piercing)
Speed Factor: 6
Proficiency Type: Spear
Type: Two-handed
Requires:
 5 Strength

Weight: 5"


	SAY NAME2 "Backbiter Spear +3"
	SAY DESC "This weapon will appear as a magical spear; however when a combat situation arises, the wielder will attack an enemy and Backbiter will attack the wielder. For every attack made, there's a chance Backbiter will attack the foe and also the wielder. This is a powerful spear, but one must ask if it is worth it in the end.

STATISTICS:

Combat abilities:
– 20% Chance the wielder receives 3 points of damage (piercing) by the spear upon every successful hit

THAC0: +3
Damage: 1d8+3 (piercing)
Speed Factor: 3
Proficiency Type: Spear
Type: Two-handed
Requires:
 5 Strength

Weight: 2" 



//SPEAR OF THE UNICORN +2 - 5500mo - no evil//
COPY "rick_bigg_mod/items/SPER07.itm" "override"
	SAY NAME1 "Spear"
	SAY UNIDENTIFIED_DESC "One of the earliest weapons, dating back to the most primitive of times, the first spears were simply wooden poles or sticks sharpened at one end. When the civilized races mastered metals, spearheads were made from iron and steel. Having reached this end, weaponsmiths began experimenting with different types of spearheads, thus leading to the development of certain polearm types.

STATISTICS:

Damage: 1d6 (piercing)
Speed Factor: 6
Proficiency Type: Spear
Type: Two-handed
Requires:
 5 Strength

Weight: 5"


	SAY NAME2 "Spear of the Unicorn +2"
	SAY DESC "This graceful spear is carved to resemble the elongated horn of the unicorn. Wielders of this spear are immune to charm and hold spells, just as a unicorn might be. Whether the horn is or isn't an actual unicorn horn is the subject of much debate.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities: 
– Immunity to charm and hold
– Save vs. Death: +2

THAC0: +2
Damage: 1d6+2 (piercing)
Speed Factor: 4
Proficiency Type: Spear
Type: Two-handed
Requires:
 5 Strength

Weight: 3" 




